.\"Man page for declutter, by Dave Henderson.
.TH declutter 1 "2026 May 22"
.SH NAME
\fIdecluter\fR - data management




.SH SYNOPSIS

.B declutter [OPTIONS] ACTION SOURCE [TARGET] [STORED]

ACTIONS:
  -a   archives data
          - the TARGET value is not used
  -d   deduplicates data
          - the TARGET value can be used for comparison between dirs,
            otherwise the SOURCE will be deduplicated
  -e   cleans empty directories
          - the TARGET value is not used
  -m   cleans mismatched data
          - the SOURCE needs to contain the desired data (clean)
          - the TARGET needs to contain the additional data (dirty)

  --help      shows this screen
  --version   displays the software version

OPTIONS:
  -A   ignore data after this date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
  -B   ignore data before this date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
  -D   use and existing deduplication database: NAME
  -H   include hidden files and folders
  -P   directory prefix to remove when moving data: PREFIX
  -Y   perform a trial run with no changes made (dryrun)




